<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Vernissage Home (SPEC 6, boards 01 / 02 / 03): three rooms (Tonight, Still on the easel, New in the collection),
	the five-icon rail, the back office, the Now playing card. Everything is generated by _src/make_home.py ->
	Includes_Home.xml (ids, geometry and focus map: docs/skin.vernissage/screens/Home.md).

	Focus map (short)
	  walls 9101 / 9110-9112 / 9120-9123: Left / Right walk the works (stop at the ends; a two-part wall hops between
	    its parts), Up / Down = the previous / next room with works, Down from the last room = the rail; Back = the rail
	    (numeric). Tonight Up = the Now playing card while music plays.
	  rail 9000: Left / Right walk it (no wrap), Up = the room on show, OK opens the section (Settings: the back office
	    9130). No onback: the rail is where Back rests (SPEC 6.1), so repeated Back always ends here and never bounces.
	  back office 9130: Left / Right, Up = the room, Down / Back = the rail; cards 9131 / 9132: Up on the first row /
	    Left / Back = the back office.
	  While anything plays Kodi takes Back on Home first (CGUIWindowHome::OnAction, LESSONS): every control here also
	  leaves with Up / Down.
	Open: <defaultcontrol> is NOT "always", so coming back Kodi restores the control (and room) you left; the walls
	fill after onload, so Timers.xml hands focus to the room on show when its works arrive (vn_home_*).
	Draw order: the room -> the walls (light, works, placards, titles) -> clock / Now playing -> rail -> back office ->
	cards (after everything they cover, LESSONS Groove pass 2). Window fades sit on the content group, never on the room.
-->
<window>
	<defaultcontrol>9101</defaultcontrol>
	<menucontrol>9000</menucontrol>
	<backgroundcolor>wall_static</backgroundcolor>
	<!-- the first Home visit after Kodi starts (Startup.xml raises vn.home.first): Timers.xml vn_home_first hands
	     focus to Tonight once it fills; leaving Home ends it -->
	<onunload>ClearProperty(vn.home.first,home)</onunload>
	<controls>
		<include>VN_Room</include>
		<control type="group">
			<include>Anim_WindowContent</include>
			<include>Home_Rooms</include>
			<include>VN_Clock</include>
			<include content="VN_NowPlaying">
				<param name="nav" value="Home_NowPlayingNav"/>
			</include>
			<include>Home_Rail</include>
			<include>Home_BackOffice</include>
			<include>Home_Cards</include>
		</control>
	</controls>
</window>
